<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">ask</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">ask</ansi> command speaks to your companion, a creature bound to you.
You type your words, and a companion that can hold a conversation
answers in its own way. Most companions cannot talk, and they only look
at you.

To speak with anyone else, use <ansi fg="command">talk</ansi>. It shows you what they can tell
you as a numbered list. If you <ansi fg="command">ask</ansi> someone who is not a companion, the
game reminds you to use <ansi fg="command">talk</ansi> and nothing else happens. See
<ansi fg="command">help talk</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">ask</ansi> <ansi fg="cyan"><companion></ansi> <ansi fg="yellow"><words></ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">Examples: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">ask wolf where did you come from</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask wolf about the old road</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also: </ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">help talk</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help companion</ansi>

You can sometimes overhear townspeople chatting with each other. Pause
in busy rooms to catch the gossip.
